ck-sysdeps-solaris: a console without virtual terminals has VT 1 active

On a system whose console does not support VTs (the OBP console on SPARC,
e.g. an Ultra 45 with an XVR-300), VT_GETSTATE on /dev/vt/active fails
with EINVAL. ck_get_active_console_num() then reported VT 0, which maps to
/dev/vt/0, a device no session uses. So when a user session was added to
the static seat, no session was found on the active console and
find_possible_session_to_activate() requested the seat's LoginWindow
session again: GDM started a second X server on the display in use (it
failed: "Server is already active for display 0"), kept that display for
the login window, and after the user logged out the request for a new
greeter hit it ("Got console request to add display for session that
already has a display, and display is already in use"): no greeter came
back. The user session also stayed inactive.

Treat EINVAL/ENOTTY/ENXIO from VT_GETSTATE like the build without VT
support already does: VT 1, i.e. /dev/console, is active. Systems with VTs
(x86 with the framebuffer console) are not affected: VT_GETSTATE succeeds
there. handle_vt_active() no longer compares an uninitialised number when
VT_GETSTATE fails.

Upstream: ConsoleKit is no longer maintained (last release 0.4.6); the
Solaris code is OpenIndiana's (patches 01-28).

--- ConsoleKit-0.4.6/src/ck-sysdeps-solaris.c.orig
+++ ConsoleKit-0.4.6/src/ck-sysdeps-solaris.c
@@ -496,6 +496,20 @@
 
         res = ioctl (console_fd, VT_GETSTATE, &stat);
         if (res == ERROR) {
+                if (errno == EINVAL || errno == ENOTTY || errno == ENXIO) {
+                        /*
+                         * The console has no virtual terminals (e.g. the
+                         * OBP console on SPARC): as without VT support,
+                         * VT 1 = "/dev/console" is the active one.
+                         * Reporting 0 instead matched no session, so
+                         * every login requested a second login window
+                         * on the display already in use.
+                         */
+                        g_debug ("Console without VTs, using /dev/console");
+                        active = 1;
+                        ret = TRUE;
+                        goto out;
+                }
                 perror ("ioctl VT_GETSTATE");
                 goto out;
         }
--- ConsoleKit-0.4.6/src/ck-vt-monitor.c.orig
+++ ConsoleKit-0.4.6/src/ck-vt-monitor.c
@@ -186,6 +186,7 @@
                 num = state.v_active;
         } else {
                 g_debug ("Fails to ioctl VT_GETSTATE");
+                num = vt_monitor->priv->active_num;
         }
 
         if (vt_monitor->priv->active_num != num) {
